### Module Structure Pattern
Every module follows this exact pattern:
- Controller  → handles HTTP, calls Service, returns ApiResponse
- Service     → all business logic
- DTO         → typed data carrier (fromArray() static method)
- Request     → validation rules (extends BaseRequest)
- Routes      → api.php loaded in main routes/api.php

### Database Schema (PostgreSQL)
Tables:
- users          → id, name, email, password, role(admin/editor), timestamps
- cities         → id, name, slug, state, zip_code, description, meta_title, meta_desc, status, timestamps
- services       → id, parent_id(self FK), name, slug, description, icon, meta_title, meta_desc, sort_order, status, timestamps
- city_service   → id, city_id(FK), service_id(FK) [pivot]
- projects       → id, city_id(FK), service_id(FK), title, slug, description, location_address, is_featured, status, meta_title, meta_desc, timestamps
- project_media  → id, project_id(FK), type(before/after/video), file_path, file_type, sort_order, created_at
- blogs          → id, user_id(FK), title, slug, content, excerpt, thumbnail, status, published_at, meta_title, meta_desc, timestamps
- reviews        → id, project_id(FK nullable), customer_name, rating, review_text, source(google/manual), status, created_at
- team_members   → id, name, role, bio, photo, department, sort_order, status, timestamps
- leads          → id, name, email, phone, message, service_id(FK nullable), source_page, status(new/read/done), created_at
- materials      → id, name, slug, description, image, sort_order, status, timestamps
- site_settings  → id, key, value, group, timestamps

### Auth
- Laravel Sanctum token-based auth
- Admin only access
- role field: 'admin' | 'editor'
- Register requires ADMIN_SECRET_KEY from .env

### API Routes (current)
All routes prefixed with /api
Auth module (app/Modules/Auth/Routes/api.php):
  POST   /api/auth/admin/register   → public (requires secret_key)
  POST   /api/auth/admin/login      → public
  POST   /api/auth/admin/logout     → sanctum protected
  GET    /api/auth/admin/profile    → sanctum protected
  PUT    /api/auth/admin/password   → sanctum protected

### Coding Conventions
- Method names: camelCase (e.g. changePassword not ChangePassword)
- Always use DTOs to pass data into services
- Always return ApiResponse::success() or ApiResponse::error() from controllers
- Requests extend BaseRequest
- All new features follow the same module pattern (Controller/DTO/Request/Routes/Service)
- No business logic in controllers
- No direct Request access in services (use DTOs)

